================================================================================
!! DO NOT CITE THESE BETA VALUES EITHER -- four defects found on inspection !!
================================================================================
This is the RE-RUN on the first-peak observable, after O7 invalidated the
sup_t Omega version above. It is also not usable, for different reasons:

1. THE TWO ENSTROPHY CONVENTIONS DISAGREE ON THE CONCLUSION.
   [sum] CIs overlap  -> not distinguishable
   [max] CIs disjoint -> distinguishable
   Audit ruling O1 ("record both") exists precisely to surface this, and it
   did. A result that depends on which convention is chosen is not a result.

2. THE VISCOUS max-CONVENTION DATA IS SATURATING, NOT A POWER LAW.
   supOm_max runs 0.686, 0.766, 0.861, 0.925, 0.969, 1.003, 1.027, 1.043 --
   approaching an asymptote near ~1.05. Fitting a straight line in log-log to
   saturating data yields beta[max] = -0.168, which describes the fit, not the
   physics. The r^2 of 0.9069 -- the lowest in the run -- is the guard
   correctly signalling this.

3. THE DISPERSIVE sum-COLUMN IS NON-MONOTONIC.
   D=0.035 -> 55.019 but D=0.025 -> 48.232, i.e. LOWER at smaller D.
   Diagnosed: the number of local maxima before t=2 grows as D decreases
   (1, 2, 2, 3 at D = 0.05, 0.035, 0.025, 0.018), so "the first peak" is NOT
   the same physical feature at every D. At D=0.025 the detector catches a
   newly-appeared earlier, smaller peak (t=1.20, 48.2) rather than the later
   one it caught at D=0.035 (t=1.52, 55.0).

   => first_peak is HORIZON-robust (it fixes O7) but DISCONTINUOUS in the
      swept parameter. A new local maximum appearing shifts the measured
      value abruptly. That is a defect of the same seriousness as O7.

4. THE N-INDEPENDENCE CHECK PRINTED ABOVE IS INVALID.
   It still evaluates sup_Omega, the observable O7 retracted, so the growth
   it shows (72 -> 223 -> 327 -> 329) is the O7 horizon artifact rather than a
   statement about grid resolution. It must be re-done on whatever observable
   is finally adopted.

Candidate successor under evaluation: sup over a PRE-REGISTERED FINITE WINDOW,
max_{t <= T*} Omega(t) -- horizon-independent by construction and continuous in
the swept parameter, hence immune to both O7 and defect 3 above. See
exploration/windowed_sup_check.py.
